style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Key =
Status/Updates:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>YP 4.0.7 and YP 4.2 M2 are in =
QA<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We switched to the 6.1 kernel =
by default for M2. Unfortunately there are a couple of intermittent =
issues that seem to have crept in. One is a reproducibility issue in =
perf, likely with some host component causing it as it only occurs on =
second builds. The second appears to be an intermittent networking issue =
accessing a python http-server for testing dnf which appeared after the =
kernel version change.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We are continuing to see other =
intermittent failures which are limiting how quickly we can merge =
changes. A summary of some of the key issues was sent to the mailing =
list: <a =
href=3D"https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-core/message/176476=
"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://lists.openembedded.org/g/openembedded-cor=
e/message/176476</span></a><o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There have been changes to the =
way the codeparser cache in bitbake stores data which should reduce =
cache size, reduce the times data needs to be written out and generally =
help performance.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>CVE levels in master are still =
high but there are patches in progress for most issues as I understand =
it.<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l2 level1 =
lfo8;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>We have a growing number of =
bugs in bugzilla, any help with them is =
appreciated.<o:p></o:p></span></li></ul><p =
class=3DMsoNormal><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></p><p style=3D'margin:0in'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif;color:black'>Ways to =
contribute:</span><o:p></o:p></p><ul =
style=3D'margin-top:0in;padding-inline-start:48px' type=3Ddisc><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>As people are likely aware, the =
project has a number of components which are either unmaintained, or =
have people with little to no time trying to keep them alive. These =
components include: patchtest, layerindex, devtool, toaster, wic, oeqa, =
autobuilder, CROPs containers, pseudo and more. Many have open bugs. =
Help is welcome in trying to better look after these =
components!<o:p></o:p></span></li><li =
style=3D'color:black;margin-top:0in;margin-bottom:0in;mso-list:l0 level1 =
lfo9;vertical-align:baseline'><span =
style=3D'font-family:"Arial",sans-serif'>There are bugs identified as =
possible for newcomers to the project: <a =
href=3D"https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers"><span =
style=3D'color:#1155CC'>https://wiki.yoctoproject.org/wiki/Newcomers</spa=
